      "id": "ADV-001",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "content": "The derivative of f(x) = x³ - 6x² + 9x - 2 at x = 2 is:",
      "options": [
        {"id": "A", "text": "-3"},
        {"id": "B", "text": "0"},
        {"id": "C", "text": "3"},
        {"id": "D", "text": "6"}
      ],
      "correct_answer": "A",
      "explanation": "f'(x) = 3x² - 12x + 9. At x = 2: f'(2) = 3(4) - 12(2) + 9 = 12 - 24 + 9 = -3.",
      "difficulty": "advanced",
      "topics": ["calculus", "derivatives"]
    },
    {
      "id": "ADV-002",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "content": "In a regular pentagon, what is the measure of each interior angle?",
      "options": [
        {"id": "A", "text": "108°"},
        {"id": "B", "text": "120°"},
        {"id": "C", "text": "135°"},
        {"id": "D", "text": "144°"}
      ],
      "correct_answer": "A",
      "explanation": "For a regular n-gon, each interior angle = (n-2)×180°/n. For pentagon: (5-2)×180°/5 = 540°/5 = 108°.",
      "difficulty": "advanced", 
